":0.01847,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.091,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":9.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"WESCO International, Inc. provides business-to-business distribution, logistics services, and supply chain solutions in the United States, Canada, and internationally. It operates through three segments: Electrical & Electronic Solutions (EES), Communications & Security Solutions (CSS), and Utility & Broadband Solutions (UBS). The EES segment offers electrical equipment and supplies, automation and connected devices, security, lighting, wire and cable, and safety, as well as maintenance, repair, and operating (MRO) products. This segment also offers project execution solutions, direct and indirect manufacturing supply chain optimization programs, lighting and renewables advisory services, and digital and automation solutions. The CSS segment provides data center, network infrastructure, and security solutions. This segment sells products directly to security and network, professional audio/visual, and systems integrators, as well as data communications contractors. It also provides professional A/V, safety, facilities, and energy management solutions. The UBS segment offers products and services to investor-owned utilities, electric power cooperatives and municipalities, service and wireless providers, broadband operators, and contractors. This segment's products include wires and cables, transformers, transmission and distribution hardware, switches, protective devices, connectors, lighting and connectivity products, conduits, fiber and power cables, pole line hardware, racks, cabinets, safety and MRO products, and wireless devices. It also offers fiber project management, high and medium voltage project design and support, pre-wired meters and capacitor banks, meter testing and advanced metering infrastructure installation, personal protective equipment, dielectric testing, and tool repair, as well as emergency response, storage yard, materials, and logistics management solutions. The company was founded in 1922 and is headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John J. Engel | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["WESCO International, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $14.2B market cap on $23.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $25M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.20\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 56% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5581153930174484},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (91% sell ratio, net $7.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Wesco International (WCC) is a Top-Ranked Value Stock: Should You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024307/wesco-international-wcc-is-a-top-ranked-value-stock-should-you-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_value_score-3024307","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793886003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Wesco (NYSE:WCC) Extend Growth Across the S&P 500?